executionContract.intendedBehavior:
A worker resumed with a LANDING-CONFLICT: or LANDING-RETRY: prompt reads, in docs/roles/worker.reference.md, the same rule that the wrapper's prompt now carries (task-b5c8fd34):
- edit files only, with no new plan;
- git stays read-only: only git status, git diff, git log, git show, git ls-files and git rev-parse may run;
- every git write stays forbidden;
- HEAD can lack the merged target, so a verification snapshot built from HEAD is built from the worktree's tracked files instead.
The doc quotes the landed rule verbatim, so the doc and both prompts cannot disagree. The daemon's vendored copy (initFiles.ts ROLE_DOCS and SHIPPED_ROLE_BODY_SHAS) matches the edited doc.
